Z||000000||BAM-BAM||04-16-2000||02:20 PM||||   How rare is the engraved plenum? I found one in a wrecking yard and was thinking of picking it up if it might have some added value.<P> Thanx, BAM-BAM  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000001||Shiner||04-16-2000||03:23 PM||||I belive it came on 87-88 cars only.  I know my '87GT has the engraved plenum.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||04-16-2000||04:30 PM||||I wouldn't really call it rare.  All '87-88 V6 cars should have it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||04-16-2000||09:35 PM||||if yours doesn't have it I'd add it. May not, likely won't, add value but sure as hell looks better.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||04-17-2000||01:10 PM||||My 85se doesn't have the engraved plenum.  When I repainted the plenum I installed one of Rodney's replacement stickers.  It looks great.||||reg||1
Z||000005||stimpy||04-17-2000||07:44 PM||||Diffrent strokes for different folks... I kinda favor the plain plenum for the customzing potential. The engraved does look cool but I would not spend large amounts of money to buy one, plus it seems to me it would be fussy to keep clean.  I did a cool thing to mine... I got a V.6.-H.O. badge that you see on the front fender of 99-2K Grand Ams and plunked it right on to the top where that nasty old sticker used to be. Good wow factor, peel and stick installation, and only cost $7 from the dealer. <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=258191&a=1921599&p=16712520&Sequence=0" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=258191&a=1921599&p=16712520&Sequence=0</A> <p>[This message has been edited by stimpy (edited 04-17-2000).]||||reg||1
